long_description:
ClaimGate is a publish gate for AI-assisted marketing copy. Give it a draft and whatever evidence you already hold - a policy page, a study abstract, a price list, a product spec - and it reports:

* every claim in the draft that needs substantiation (statistics, percentages, superlatives, comparisons, guarantees, named sources, dated facts, causal statements);
* the ones it cannot tie to any evidence you supplied;
* the rules of your own policy the draft breaks, blocked outright if they are prohibited-claims rules;
* whether a required AI disclosure (EU AI Act Article 50) is missing from customer-facing AI-assisted copy.

It fails closed. If it cannot decide a claim it returns `unverified`, never `supported` - and `unverified` blocks, because a gate that waves through what it could not check is decoration. A number in a claim that appears in no evidence is caught by a plain string comparison with no model consulted, because a fabricated figure is not a judgement call.

It is a checker, not a writer. It does not browse, does not invent facts, and does not write your copy.

MIT licensed, source and test suite public: https://github.com/caseone115/claimgate

Disclosure: this software is written and maintained by automated software.
